{"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Sending-to-Snowplow","title":"Sending to Snowplow","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowSetupError"]},{"anchor":"Encoding-batches","title":"Encoding batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder"]},{"anchor":"Records-left-out","title":"Records left out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowEncodingError"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to a Snowplow collector as self-describing events, whose schemas come from the tracking plan."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" makes an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") for a Snowplow pipeline in one call. It checks the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"collector’s URL, the Iglu vendor and the app ID, and posts to the collector’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/com.snowplowanalytics.snowplow\/tp2"},{"type":"text","text":" endpoint with a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". It splits each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"batch to the limits of Snowplow’s own mobile trackers ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"): 25"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events and 40,000 bytes a request, with a larger event, of up to 150,000 bytes, in a request of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its own. A batch with no record the encoder can write, an empty one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"included, makes no request. The destination retries no response, a 5xx, 408 and 429, and drops"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and reports any other status. No trace context is sent. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" leaves this module out;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"import it on its own."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A collector takes events from anyone who can reach it, so there is no key or secret, and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination builds on every platform: an app sends to the collector directly."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import HTTPDestinations","import SnowplowEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let snowplow = try HTTPDestination.snowplow(","    collector: collector,  \/\/ https:\/\/collector.example.com","    vendor: \"com.example\",  \/\/ the Iglu vendor the plan is exported under","    appID: \"shop-ios\",","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: snowplow)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The factory throws "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowSetupError"},{"type":"text","text":" for a collector URL that isn’t "},{"code":"https","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", that has no host,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a user name, a query or a fragment, or that already ends in the endpoint; for a vendor Iglu"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"doesn’t take; and for an empty app ID or one longer than 255 UTF-16 code units."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Schemas from the tracking plan","anchor":"Schemas-from-the-tracking-plan"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each event is a self-describing event: its data comes with the Iglu URI of the schema it must"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"match, and Snowplow’s pipeline validates it against that schema before loading it. The URI is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"named after the event and its version, under the vendor the destination is given:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["iglu:<vendor>\/<name>\/jsonschema\/<version>-0-0"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Version N of an event is SchemaVer ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"N-0-0"},{"text":", and events always name it. Raising an event’s version","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a breaking change, which is SchemaVer’s MODEL. The export compares each event with the newest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"schema of its version the registry holds, by what the two mean rather than their bytes, as the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"plan’s own check does:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An event that hasn’t changed keeps its published file, and nothing is written."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A breaking change at the same version, such as a property made required, is refused: raise the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event’s version."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A compatible change, such as an optional property added, is an ADDITION. For Iglu Server the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"export writes it as ","type":"text"},{"code":"N-0-1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", then ","type":"text"},{"code":"N-0-2","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", each listing the earlier ones in ","type":"text"},{"code":"$supersedes","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Snowplow validates events naming ","type":"text"},{"code":"N-0-0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" against the newest, so a release already in users’","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hands keeps validating. Superseding needs Iglu Server 0.11.0 or later and Enrich 3.8.0 or later.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A static repository doesn’t support it: it would validate those events against ","type":"text"},{"code":"N-0-0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" alone,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so for one the export refuses the change, and the event needs a new version.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Write the registry from the plan with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan.writeIgluRegistry(to:vendor:registry:)"},{"type":"text","text":", the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"iglu <vendor> server|static <registry-directory>"},{"type":"text","text":" command of the tracking plan’s executable, or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"export-tracking-plan"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"--iglu-vendor"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"--iglu-registry"},{"type":"text","text":". Then publish it with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"igluctl"},{"type":"text","text":" before the release that sends the events."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An event name Iglu takes holds only ASCII letters, digits, ","type":"text"},{"code":"-","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"_","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and the version must be 1","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or more. The encoder skips every record of an event that breaks either rule, and logs a notice for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each such event of the plan when the destination is made. The export refuses such an event too.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"What Snowplow receives","anchor":"What-Snowplow-receives"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each request is a ","type":"text"},{"code":"payload_data","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" 1-0-4 array of events, one per record. Every event has:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"e","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"ue","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": a self-describing event, with its data in "},{"code":"ue_pr","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" as JSON text;"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"eid"},{"text":", the record’s identifier, which a redelivered record keeps;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"dtm","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"ttm","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the record’s timestamp in milliseconds, so Snowplow’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"derived_tstamp","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is when","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the event was tracked;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"aid"},{"text":", the app ID; ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"text":", the platform; ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tv"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"traffluent"},{"text":"; and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ip"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0.0.0.0"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stm"},{"type":"text","text":" is sent: a retried request sends the same body again, so a sent time would be the first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attempt’s, and Snowplow would move the event later by however long the retries took."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The standard context, when the record has it, goes in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"co"},{"type":"text","text":" as Snowplow’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mobile_context"},{"type":"text","text":" 1-0-3"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(the operating system, Apple as the manufacturer, the device model, the network type and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"language) and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"application"},{"type":"text","text":" 1-0-0 (the app’s version and build). The platform is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mob"},{"type":"text","text":" for a phone,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pad, watch or Vision Pro, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tv"},{"type":"text","text":" for an Apple TV, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pc"},{"type":"text","text":" for a Mac and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"app"},{"type":"text","text":" for a record with no device."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the ","type":"text"},{"code":"TrackingPlan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the encoder is made with. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Only the session identifies a record","anchor":"Only-the-session-identifies-a-record"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s session, from the sessions enricher, is its ","type":"text"},{"code":"sid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", Snowplow’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"domain_sessionid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nothing else identifies it. No ","type":"text"},{"code":"duid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"uid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"nuid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"tnuid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is sent, no ","type":"text"},{"code":"client_session","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"entity (its ","type":"text"},{"code":"userId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lasts across sessions), and no IDFV, IDFA or other device identifier. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record’s vendor identifier and trace context aren’t sent either. A record with no session, from a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tracker without the sessions enricher, is sent without a ","type":"text"},{"code":"sid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; a record a store recovered after a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"relaunch keeps its session and its ","type":"text"},{"code":"sid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Snowplow’s mobile data models","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"read a session from the ","type":"text"},{"code":"client_session","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" entity, so set the unified package’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"snowplow__session_identifiers","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to ","type":"text"},{"code":"[{\"schema\": \"atomic\", \"field\": \"domain_sessionid\"}]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for these","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The collector would give each device an identifier of its own: it sets an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sp"},{"type":"text","text":" cookie, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps and sends back, and records the request’s IP address. Every request carries"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SP-Anonymous: *"},{"type":"text","text":", so the collector sets and reads no cookie, records "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"network_userid"},{"type":"text","text":" as all"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"zeros, and records no IP address or forwarding header fields."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Records left out","anchor":"Records-left-out"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out and the rest of the batch is sent:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"one the plan doesn’t describe, whose event isn’t ","type":"text"},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or that holds a value JSON can’t;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose event name Iglu doesn’t take, or whose version is below 1;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"one whose timestamp falls outside the years 0 to 9999, which Snowplow’s enrichment fails;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose JSON is over 150,000 bytes, which the smallest of a pipeline’s streams, SQS’s 192 kB,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"might not take with the request around it."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The destination reports each as ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a ","type":"text"},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" whose reason is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowEncodingError","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"What the collector doesn’t report","anchor":"What-the-collector-doesnt-report"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The collector answers 200 to every request it can read and validates nothing. Snowplow checks the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events later, in enrichment. An event whose data its schema rejects, whose schema the pipeline’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Iglu resolver can’t find, or that is larger than the pipeline’s stream takes, becomes a failed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event: it is kept apart and never reaches the warehouse, though the destination counted it as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivered. Publish each schema before the release that sends it, and watch the pipeline’s failed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events after a change to the plan. Snowplow’s resolver caches schemas, for 10 minutes by default,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so a schema published after the first event that names it can still be missed for that long.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Snowplow doesn’t remove duplicates as events arrive. A record is sent more than once when a request","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is retried after the collector stored it but the answer was lost, when a delivery sends a cancelled","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"batch again, and when a store redelivers records after a relaunch. Each copy keeps its ","type":"text"},{"code":"eid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Snowplow’s data models, which deduplicate on ","type":"text"},{"code":"event_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", count it once.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers what Snowplow receives, and why, in more detail.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/snowplowencoding"]}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework","title":"SnowplowEncoding","externalID":"SnowplowEncoding","modules":[{"name":"SnowplowEncoding"}],"role":"collection"},"references":{"doc://SnowplowEncoding/documentation/SnowplowEncoding":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to a Snowplow collector as self-describing events, whose schemas come from the tracking plan."}],"url":"\/documentation\/snowplowencoding","role":"collection","type":"topic","title":"SnowplowEncoding","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding"},"doc://SnowplowEncoding/documentation/SnowplowEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:backoff:clock:)":{"conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transport"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSessionTransport"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encoding"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SnowplowBatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"snowplow"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"collector"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials3URLV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"URL"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"vendor"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"appID"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"plan"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"TrackingPlan"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"backoff"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations18ExponentialBackoffV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ExponentialBackoff"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"clock"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Clock"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Duration"},{"kind":"text","text":">) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16SnowplowEncoding0A10SetupErrorO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SnowplowSetupError"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations15HTTPDestinationV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"HTTPDestination"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations19URLSessionTransportV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"URLSessionTransport"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16SnowplowEncoding0A12BatchEncoderV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SnowplowBatchEncoder"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A destination that sends batches to the Snowplow collector at ","type":"text"},{"code":"collector","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as self-describing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events whose schemas are ","type":"text"},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s under ","type":"text"},{"code":"vendor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", from the app ","type":"text"},{"code":"appID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"URLSession.shared","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", retrying a send that fails for now with the waits of ","type":"text"},{"code":"backoff","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"clock","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:backoff:clock:)","title":"snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:backoff:clock:)","url":"\/documentation\/snowplowencoding\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appid:plan:backoff:clock:)"},"doc://SnowplowEncoding/documentation/SnowplowEncoding/SnowplowBatchEncoder/batchLimit":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"batchLimit"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"BatchLimit","preciseIdentifier":"s:12PropertyJSON10BatchLimitV"}],"url":"\/documentation\/snowplowencoding\/snowplowbatchencoder\/batchlimit","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","kind":"symbol","role":"sym